                <pb facs="0776" n="658" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg658"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.77/252: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-11-13T12:00:00-05:45">November 13,
                        1929—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:55 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>271. I laid your telegram 159, November 12, 3 p.m., before President Moncada last
                    night. He has just told me that he would immediately give Dr. Sacasa cabled
                    instructions in the matter and direct him to say that it was not the intention
                    of the Government of Nicaragua to proceed in an illegal manner when it issued
                    the decree reported upon in my 268, November 9, 1 p.m., nor to terminate its
                    contract with the railway management.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
